Z||000002||olympic||07-25-2000||07:34 PM||||  My computer(a Pentium 100) was getting so bad for locking up and crashing that I finally said screw it and reformatted my hard drive.  I saved anything I thought I might need and then after reformatting I reloaded Windows 98 and spent about 10 hours downloading Netscape and a bunch of other upgrades and plug-ins.  Everything worked great except for that certificate problem which I have fixed now.  The strange thing is that before my hard drive had about 1.6 gigs stored on it and now it only has 300 megs.  And I basically have the same stuff loaded now as I did before.  So something was taking up 1.3 gigs that was of no use.  Oh well, everything is fine now.<P>   BTW, I see Netscape has released the preview of Communicator 6, has anyone tried it?  Any comments, reviews?<P>------------------<BR>Your best...???  Losers whine about doing their best.   Winners go home and f*** the prom queen! - Sean Connery in "The Rock"||||reg||1
